Description: Let GNOME Shell tell GTK that it shows the menu bars of windows.
 GTK hides the menu bar of a GtkApplicationWindow when the compositor announces the gtk_shell1 capability
 GLOBAL_MENU_BAR, which mutter never announces. meta_display_set_shell_shows_menubar() adds the capability and
 sends the capabilities to all clients again, and unsetting it removes the capability, after which GTK shows
 the menu bars again.
 .
 The test wayland-gtk-shell-menubar checks that a client receives the capability when it is set, once only,
 and loses it when it is unset, and that a client which binds gtk_shell1 while it is set receives it at
 once.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-24
